322: calling/lint repair, commit, push, upload, migration or deployment was performed.  1: # DoloGram Messenger-style mobile search implementation plan
  2: 
  3: Prepared and polished on 2026-11-11, Asia/Manila.
  4: 
  5: **Status — second-pass audit complete. Ready for execution when implementation is requested. Implementation and operational verification have not started.** This audit edits only this document and its [context index](context/DoloGram_Search_Context_Index.md). The user's standing emulator/testing authorization applies throughout later execution. This planning-only request does not start execution.
  6: 
  7: ## 1. Goal, scope, and evidence labels
  8: 
  9: Reproduce the Messenger search experience through recent searches, grouped conversation results, scoped message snippets, and navigation to the original message. Global and scoped search share matching and presentation rules. Preserve DoloGram's existing account isolation, offline cache, chat organization, Markdown, and navigation behavior.
 10: 
 11: **Verified** identifies current source inspection. **Reported** identifies historical evidence that needs revalidation. **Proposed** identifies the executable behavior selected by this plan. **Unresolved** identifies a prerequisite with a consequence and next action in Section 9. All implementation requirements and acceptance criteria below are proposed work.
 12: 
 13: The visual adaptation carries forward the earlier plan's DoloGram charcoal/ivory palette, Inter typography, and existing icons. Messenger supplies the screen hierarchy, rounded field, avatar-led rows, recent-history management, and conversation-first message retrieval. All/People/Groups/Messages filters and the ranking rules are DoloGram design choices. The research does not verify those exact controls on every current Messenger build.
 14: 
 15: Supported execution target is the existing Android Expo app on the assigned MuMu Player instance named `dologram`, package `com.dologram.app`, using ADB only. Shared React Native code must retain its existing iOS branches and type compatibility. Physical-device and iOS-device testing are not prerequisites under the recorded emulator-only restriction.
 16: 
 17: Feature scope covers local synced messages, currently eligible contacts/groups, recent history, the existing exact-username lookup, snippets, highlighting, and historical navigation. Shared media browsing remains the existing chat-info destination. Full-name remote directory discovery, assistant answers, OCR, audio transcription, original-filename search, new date/sender filters, new backend APIs, schema migrations, unrelated navigation redesign, and calling work require separate scope. The existing media model supplies attachment-type labels and has no original-filename column.
 18: 
 19: ## 2. Working-copy baseline and verified findings
 20: 
 21: The working copy is the baseline. `git status --short` shows most application, shared, schema, and plan directories as untracked. Tracked and staged diff statistics are empty. `git ls-files` lists README and older documentation files, so committed history cannot restore the current application. Preserve relevant untracked inputs before execution. This request modified no application files. Concurrent calling work changed manifests, app configuration, shared strings, and root route integration during inspection. Their search-relevant contracts were rechecked and their latest identities are recorded in the context index. Revalidate those identities again at execution start.
 22: 
 23: | Finding | Current source and implication |
 24: |---|---|
 25: | Global search already searches beyond 200 rows | `apps/mobile/app/search.tsx` and `src/search/query.ts` use 150 ms message-search debounce, 200-row scan batches, 30-match pages, `(createdAt, messageId)` cursors, Unicode NFKC normalization, nickname/type matching, and AbortController checks. Extend these paths. |
 26: | Scoped search has a different data window and error behavior | `apps/mobile/app/chat/[chatId]/search.tsx` reads `loadChatSnapshot(..., { limit: 200 })`, includes pending queue items from the snapshot, swallows read errors, and replaces itself when opening a result. Remove the history limit and silent failure while retaining supported pending-message behavior. |
 27: | Membership and organization already affect search | `useChatList` returns active, archived, and ignored items, excludes blocked chats, and uses local deleted preferences. Global search currently includes all three returned lists. Preserve these inclusion rules. |
 28: | Existing contact reads are broader than the new search needs | `src/chats/infoQuery.ts::loadCachedContacts` selects every cached member other than the caller, without joining the caller's membership or the search allowlist. Search requires a scoped adapter. Preserve the existing group-picker callers. |
 29: | Direct-chat creation already has error and conflict handling | `src/chats/directChat.ts::openDirectChat` looks up cached direct chats, then creates rows and resyncs after second-member conflicts. Reuse it, guard repeated taps, and surface its failed outcome. Its multi-row operation is not an atomic backend transaction. |
 30: | Historical navigation already exists | `src/chat/query.ts::loadChatSnapshotForMessage` loads bounded surrounding history. Missing targets fall back to the latest snapshot. The chat screen highlights a row background but currently receives no query for text highlights. Preserve helper compatibility and add explicit search-target availability feedback. |
 31: | SearchField has multiple callers | Global search, scoped search, and `app/forward.tsx` consume it. It owns internal text and passes remaining TextInput props afterward. Controlled/prefilled support must synchronize rendered text, clear-button visibility, callback timing, and internal state. |
